cff-version: 1.2.0
title: The Ladder
message: >-
  If you use this rig, or quote a number measured with it, please cite
  it. If you re-measure something and get a different answer, that is
  more useful than a citation -- please say so.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A test rig for 64-bit mixers that does not saturate. It feeds
  mixer(ror64(T(counter) xor C, r)) to PractRand under Evensen's RRC
  disguise scheme and reports the data volume at which the output can
  first be told apart from randomness. That volume is the metric: weak
  mixers give themselves away after kilobytes, strong ones hold for
  terabytes. The repository holds the instrument, eight write-ups, the
  raw measurements the write-ups rest on including the ones that went
  against the author, and a single-header reference implementation of
  the two mixers that came out of it.
authors:
